 "description": "DRAFT (2026-11-12 ~12:20, the train_filter build; ~13:50 the user's SE rule of 13:22-13:24 and cold share 1.0; NOT created). The user's Elo-filtered multi-kind experiment (11-12 ~11:11; analyst 6.85 (b)): the old global league's training rule as an experiment, for insight. train_filter {\"margin\": \"se\"} (the user, 11-12 13:22-13:24, the global league's qualify rule: \"both players need to be at least the current model's strength - standard error based on last round\"; \"cut a model's own games against significantly weaker opponents\"): line L's floor is R_L - SE_L, R_L its current version's cold Elo in this cycle's fit and SE_L that rating's standard error in the fit (its games this cycle; no averaging); a game of the local set trains L iff both players are rated at or above the floor (unrated players count), L's own games too, so its games against weaker opponents are cut (its current version against itself always passes; nothing is cut while it is unrated). self_games_topup: each line the filter cut games from plays k = min(1584, U - K) extra games, K kept of the local set's U, its current version against its champion if the champion is rated at or above the floor, else against itself (colours alternating; against itself too when it crowned this cycle), so its set returns to the local set's size, at most 1,584 more (training only, never rated; logged per line). Lines (the six of update 8 at ply 1, analyst 6.84 (2) / 6.85 (b)): F-L; F-P; T-P-Ne-grow with the leaf bar on (--grow-mdl 1 --grow-gate age --grow-priority snapshot); T-P-Ne capped (limit 4, 1M, noise 0.03); T-L-Ne capped forget 10 (limit 4, 1M). The optional sixth seat, T-L-Ne-grow-f10, is one more models row ({\"model\": \"T-L-Ne-grow-f10\"}; 6 lines: 12 entries, 12 rounds, plateau K 29); a router-split DAG seat only if grow-dag-p1 reads well against strangers (6.80's rule). Ply 1, games_per_cycle 1584 (5 lines: 10 entries, 18 double round-robins, 1,620 games), self-games, cold_games T 0.02 share 1.0 (the user, 13:22: \"play more games per round so that the standard error is lower\": 18 cold double round-robins, 1,620 games, 324 an entry, so a current version's SE is ~22-26 against ~47-55 at share 0.25 (the cold twins' current versions: median 40-47 on 98 games); every decision on the cold fit). End rule (the user's): no retirement (experiments never retire), crownings at the default 2.0 SE on the cold set (11-12 13:21: champion_se 2.5 dropped; the cold twins crowned at 2.0 as often as the T 0.1 runs, and 2.5 would have halved their crownings: z of every champion test in their cycles.csv; analyst 6.89 (a) flagged it; the user's end rule: \"just like experiments do\"), plateau scaled (K 32 for 5 lines) from cycle 300, cap 600. Seed 63 (62 is grow-dag-p1's draft). Games chessai-hybrid17; after create, before cycle 1: python3 leagues/specs/ply1/train_binary.py --from chessai-hybrid4gfx leagues/experiments/NAME chessai-hybrid6 (F-L, F-P and the capped trees; T-P-Ne-grow keeps its recipe's chessai-grow4, T-L-Ne-grow-f10 chessai-grow5). cold_games.train is \"TODO\" on purpose (create refuses it): set it from 6.82's twins (treeonly-p1-coldtrain / -coldrate, then fponly): true if the cold games may train, else false; the filtered run and its twin must carry the same value. WAITS for those twins (6.85: the filter on T 0.1 ratings is the biased one we already ran; on cold ratings it is a different experiment). Predictions (6.85 (b)), filtered minus its unfiltered twin against the standing ply-1 panel: flats 10-30 better, trees 0-40 better (6.78 (a)'s uniform-tree effect); the ranking unchanged (trees over flats by 60-110 against the mixed panel, 40-70 of it matchup); at ply 2 everything within 30. What it is for (insight, not hard conclusions): the data flows upward only, each line training on games between players at least about as strong as itself (within one SE): the flats on the trees' games too, the trees on tree-only games (treeonly-p1's regime), the top line on few games plus its top-up: do weaker kinds catch up faster from their betters' games, does the ranking stay stable, what co-adaptation does under a filter. Read: the standing ply-1 panel (r + e + g + h at v300), v150, v300 and the final, plies 1 and 2, filtered against twin line by line; each line's rating, SE, floor, own games kept, kept share and top-up games per cycle from cycles.csv (filter_* and topup_* columns). Twin: filtered-p1-twin.DRAFT.json (the same without train_filter and self_games_topup, the same seed: cycle 1's round-robins are the same games). Expected kept shares (the rule replayed on the cold twins' last 40 cycles, models/from-scratch/filter-build/sim/kept_share3.py; uniform fields of 4 lines, 8 entries): with their own SE (share 0.25, median 40-47) a line keeps 70-96% of the set on average (72-96% of its own games) and the top-up is ~700-1,650 games a cycle; with half that SE (what share 1.0 gives, the ratings' own noise left as it is, so an upper bound on the cut) 37-81%, ~2,100-3,300. Here (10 entries; rating-only cold games: U 1,800 = 1,620 round-robin games and 180 self-games) a line keeps n^2/100 of the set, n the entries rated at or above its floor; simulated with SE 20-24 (sim/mixed_se_sim.py), the trees keep ~20-33% and top up ~1,170-1,400 each if they sit 50-150 above the flats on cold ratings (likely: in-run T 0.1 bunches the kinds within ~15-35 Elo and under-rates trees by ~100-150), the flats ~80% (~330-410 each): ~4,300-4,900 top-up games a cycle; ~3,900-4,100 with no kind gap (each line ~55%). If the cold games train too, U is 3,420 and most tree lines top up the full 1,584. Cost (measured rates of the running ply-1 runs: replay-games ~1.8-2.5 ms CPU a game, cold games ~1.2-2 ms with their fit): the twin ~12 CPU-s a cycle early to ~21-24 late (cold share 1.0 adds ~2-4 CPU-s over 0.25); the top-up adds ~8-12 CPU-s; so ~20-24 CPU-s a cycle early to ~30-35 late, ~2-5 CPU-h over 300-600 cycles (the twin ~1.4-3.6).",
